@lang en
-- Tests of ie-interpretation-time.l4: periods of time (section 18(h) and the Schedule's time words).
-- Every expected value was decided by reading the quoted section and written into NOTES.md section 2 (or worked out on a calendar) BEFORE the code ran.
-- A failing assertion here is a finding about the reading; none was edited to match what the code printed.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ie-interpretation-time`

§ `A helper for the tests`

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
      u IS A `Unit of time`
      h IS A `How a period is counted`
      d IS A DATE
GIVETH A `A period of time`
`the test period` n u h d MEANS
    `A period of time` WITH
        `its length`                 IS n
        `its unit`                   IS u
        `how it is counted`          IS h
        `the day it is counted from` IS d

§ `Premises about the calendar (so a reviewer need not trust the arithmetic below)`

#ASSERT `Weekday of` (YMD 2026 1 1) EQUALS 4        -- Thursday
#ASSERT `Weekday of` (YMD 2026 1 3) EQUALS 6        -- Saturday
#ASSERT `Weekday of` (YMD 2026 1 4) EQUALS 0        -- Sunday
#ASSERT `Weekday of` (YMD 2026 1 5) EQUALS 1        -- Monday
#ASSERT `Weekday of` (YMD 2025 8 31) EQUALS 0       -- Sunday

§ `Section 18(h): N days from a day. The first day is day 1.`

-- one day: begins and ends on the same day
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of` 1 `days beginning on or reckoned from` (YMD 2026 1 1) EQUALS YMD 2026 1 1
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of` 2 `days beginning on or reckoned from` (YMD 2026 1 1) EQUALS YMD 2026 1 2
-- one week's worth of days
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of` 7 `days beginning on or reckoned from` (YMD 2026 1 1) EQUALS YMD 2026 1 7
-- thirty days (the worked case): 1 January is day 1, 30 January is day 30
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of` 30 `days beginning on or reckoned from` (YMD 2026 1 1) EQUALS YMD 2026 1 30
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of` 31 `days beginning on or reckoned from` (YMD 2026 1 1) EQUALS YMD 2026 1 31
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of` 32 `days beginning on or reckoned from` (YMD 2026 1 1) EQUALS YMD 2026 2 1
-- a start on the 31st: 31 January is day 1, 28 February is day 29, 1 March is day 30
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of` 30 `days beginning on or reckoned from` (YMD 2026 1 31) EQUALS YMD 2026 3 1
-- year ends
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of` 3 `days beginning on or reckoned from` (YMD 2025 12 30) EQUALS YMD 2026 1 1
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of` 365 `days beginning on or reckoned from` (YMD 2025 1 1) EQUALS YMD 2025 12 31
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of` 366 `days beginning on or reckoned from` (YMD 2024 1 1) EQUALS YMD 2024 12 31
-- leap day: 28 February 2024 is day 1, 29 February day 2, 1 March day 3
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of` 1 `days beginning on or reckoned from` (YMD 2024 2 28) EQUALS YMD 2024 2 28
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of` 2 `days beginning on or reckoned from` (YMD 2024 2 28) EQUALS YMD 2024 2 29
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of` 3 `days beginning on or reckoned from` (YMD 2024 2 28) EQUALS YMD 2024 3 1
-- a start on 29 February: day 365 is 27 February 2025 (28 February 2025 is day 366)
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of` 365 `days beginning on or reckoned from` (YMD 2024 2 29) EQUALS YMD 2025 2 27
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of` 366 `days beginning on or reckoned from` (YMD 2024 2 29) EQUALS YMD 2025 2 28
-- not a period: no days, a negative number, a fraction
#ASSERT REFUSED `the last day of a period of` 0 `days beginning on or reckoned from` (YMD 2026 1 1) BECAUSE "a period must be a whole number of units, at least one"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the last day of a period of` (0 MINUS 3) `days beginning on or reckoned from` (YMD 2026 1 1)
#ASSERT REFUSED `the last day of a period of` 1.5 `days beginning on or reckoned from` (YMD 2026 1 1)

§ `The boundary days on each side of a period of 30 days from 1 January 2026`

#ASSERT NOT `the day` (YMD 2025 12 31) `falls within the period beginning on` (YMD 2026 1 1) `and ending on` (YMD 2026 1 30)
#ASSERT     `the day` (YMD 2026 1 1)   `falls within the period beginning on` (YMD 2026 1 1) `and ending on` (YMD 2026 1 30)
#ASSERT     `the day` (YMD 2026 1 30)  `falls within the period beginning on` (YMD 2026 1 1) `and ending on` (YMD 2026 1 30)
#ASSERT NOT `the day` (YMD 2026 1 31)  `falls within the period beginning on` (YMD 2026 1 1) `and ending on` (YMD 2026 1 30)
#ASSERT `the number of days in the period beginning on` (YMD 2026 1 1) `and ending on` (YMD 2026 1 30) EQUALS 30
#ASSERT `the number of days in the period beginning on` (YMD 2026 1 1) `and ending on` (YMD 2026 1 1) EQUALS 1

§ `Section 18(h), second limb: a period that ends on or is reckoned to a day includes that day`

#ASSERT `the day` (YMD 2026 6 30) `falls within the period beginning on` (YMD 2026 6 1) `and ending on` (YMD 2026 6 30)
#ASSERT NOT `the day` (YMD 2026 7 1) `falls within the period beginning on` (YMD 2026 6 1) `and ending on` (YMD 2026 6 30)

§ `N weeks from a day: only from the first day of a week (a Sunday); Schedule Pt 1 "week" and "midnight"`

-- 4 January 2026 is a Sunday
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of` 1 `weeks beginning on or reckoned from` (YMD 2026 1 4) EQUALS YMD 2026 1 10
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of` 2 `weeks beginning on or reckoned from` (YMD 2026 1 4) EQUALS YMD 2026 1 17
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of` 4 `weeks beginning on or reckoned from` (YMD 2026 1 4) EQUALS YMD 2026 1 31
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of` 1 `weeks beginning on or reckoned from` (YMD 2026 1 25) EQUALS YMD 2026 1 31
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of` 2 `weeks beginning on or reckoned from` (YMD 2026 1 25) EQUALS YMD 2026 2 7
-- any other start: no rule
#ASSERT REFUSED `the last day of a period of` 1 `weeks beginning on or reckoned from` (YMD 2026 1 1) BECAUSE "the Act has no rule for a period of weeks that does not begin on a Sunday"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the last day of a period of` 1 `weeks beginning on or reckoned from` (YMD 2026 1 3)
#ASSERT REFUSED `the last day of a period of` 1 `weeks beginning on or reckoned from` (YMD 2026 1 5)
#ASSERT REFUSED `the last day of a period of` 0 `weeks beginning on or reckoned from` (YMD 2026 1 4) BECAUSE "a period must be a whole number of units, at least one"

§ `N calendar months from a day: only from the first day of a month; Schedule Pt 1 "month"`

#ASSERT `the last day of a period of` 1 `calendar months beginning on or reckoned from` (YMD 2025 1 1) EQUALS YMD 2025 1 31
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of` 1 `calendar months beginning on or reckoned from` (YMD 2025 2 1) EQUALS YMD 2025 2 28
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of` 1 `calendar months beginning on or reckoned from` (YMD 2024 2 1) EQUALS YMD 2024 2 29
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of` 1 `calendar months beginning on or reckoned from` (YMD 2025 4 1) EQUALS YMD 2025 4 30
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of` 2 `calendar months beginning on or reckoned from` (YMD 2025 1 1) EQUALS YMD 2025 2 28
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of` 2 `calendar months beginning on or reckoned from` (YMD 2024 1 1) EQUALS YMD 2024 2 29
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of` 3 `calendar months beginning on or reckoned from` (YMD 2025 1 1) EQUALS YMD 2025 3 31
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of` 6 `calendar months beginning on or reckoned from` (YMD 2025 7 1) EQUALS YMD 2025 12 31
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of` 12 `calendar months beginning on or reckoned from` (YMD 2025 1 1) EQUALS YMD 2025 12 31
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of` 13 `calendar months beginning on or reckoned from` (YMD 2025 1 1) EQUALS YMD 2026 1 31
-- across a year end
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of` 1 `calendar months beginning on or reckoned from` (YMD 2025 12 1) EQUALS YMD 2025 12 31
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of` 2 `calendar months beginning on or reckoned from` (YMD 2025 12 1) EQUALS YMD 2026 1 31
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of` 3 `calendar months beginning on or reckoned from` (YMD 2025 11 1) EQUALS YMD 2026 1 31
-- any other start (the 2nd, the 15th, the 31st, the last day of February, 29 February): no rule
#ASSERT REFUSED `the last day of a period of` 1 `calendar months beginning on or reckoned from` (YMD 2025 1 2) BECAUSE "the Act has no rule for a period of calendar months that does not begin on the first day of a month"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the last day of a period of` 1 `calendar months beginning on or reckoned from` (YMD 2025 1 15)
#ASSERT REFUSED `the last day of a period of` 1 `calendar months beginning on or reckoned from` (YMD 2025 1 31)
#ASSERT REFUSED `the last day of a period of` 1 `calendar months beginning on or reckoned from` (YMD 2025 3 31)
#ASSERT REFUSED `the last day of a period of` 1 `calendar months beginning on or reckoned from` (YMD 2025 2 28)
#ASSERT REFUSED `the last day of a period of` 1 `calendar months beginning on or reckoned from` (YMD 2024 2 29)
#ASSERT REFUSED `the last day of a period of` 0 `calendar months beginning on or reckoned from` (YMD 2025 1 1) BECAUSE "a period must be a whole number of units, at least one"

§ `N years from a day: only from 1 January; Schedule Pt 1 "year"`

#ASSERT `the last day of a period of` 1 `years beginning on or reckoned from` (YMD 2025 1 1) EQUALS YMD 2025 12 31
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of` 1 `years beginning on or reckoned from` (YMD 2024 1 1) EQUALS YMD 2024 12 31
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of` 3 `years beginning on or reckoned from` (YMD 2025 1 1) EQUALS YMD 2027 12 31
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of` 5 `years beginning on or reckoned from` (YMD 2025 1 1) EQUALS YMD 2029 12 31
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of` 1 `years beginning on or reckoned from` (YMD 2000 1 1) EQUALS YMD 2000 12 31
-- any other start: no rule
#ASSERT REFUSED `the last day of a period of` 1 `years beginning on or reckoned from` (YMD 2025 1 2) BECAUSE "the Act has no rule for a period of years that does not begin on 1 January"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the last day of a period of` 3 `years beginning on or reckoned from` (YMD 2025 7 16)
#ASSERT REFUSED `the last day of a period of` 5 `years beginning on or reckoned from` (YMD 2025 1 15)
#ASSERT REFUSED `the last day of a period of` 5 `years beginning on or reckoned from` (YMD 2025 9 1)
#ASSERT REFUSED `the last day of a period of` 2 `years beginning on or reckoned from` (YMD 2024 2 28)
#ASSERT REFUSED `the last day of a period of` 1 `years beginning on or reckoned from` (YMD 2024 2 29)
#ASSERT REFUSED `the last day of a period of` 1 `years beginning on or reckoned from` (YMD 2025 12 31)
#ASSERT REFUSED `the last day of a period of` 0 `years beginning on or reckoned from` (YMD 2025 1 1) BECAUSE "a period must be a whole number of units, at least one"

§ `A period counted after an event: section 18(h) is silent, so every unit refuses`

#ASSERT REFUSED `the last day of the period` (`the test period` 30 Days `after an event` (YMD 2026 1 1)) BECAUSE "section 18(h) says nothing about a period counted after an event"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the last day of the period` (`the test period` 1 Weeks `after an event` (YMD 2026 1 4))
#ASSERT REFUSED `the last day of the period` (`the test period` 1 `Calendar months` `after an event` (YMD 2025 1 31))
#ASSERT REFUSED `the last day of the period` (`the test period` 1 `Calendar months` `after an event` (YMD 2025 1 1))
#ASSERT REFUSED `the last day of the period` (`the test period` 1 Years `after an event` (YMD 2024 2 29))
#ASSERT REFUSED `the last day of the period` (`the test period` 1 Years `after an event` (YMD 2025 1 1))

§ `Whether a day falls within a period given as a record`

-- 30 days from 1 January 2026: the boundary days, both sides
#ASSERT NOT `the day` (YMD 2025 12 31) `falls within the period` (`the test period` 30 Days `from a day` (YMD 2026 1 1))
#ASSERT     `the day` (YMD 2026 1 1)   `falls within the period` (`the test period` 30 Days `from a day` (YMD 2026 1 1))
#ASSERT     `the day` (YMD 2026 1 30)  `falls within the period` (`the test period` 30 Days `from a day` (YMD 2026 1 1))
#ASSERT NOT `the day` (YMD 2026 1 31)  `falls within the period` (`the test period` 30 Days `from a day` (YMD 2026 1 1))
-- one month from 1 February 2025: 28 February is inside, 1 March outside, 31 January outside
#ASSERT NOT `the day` (YMD 2025 1 31) `falls within the period` (`the test period` 1 `Calendar months` `from a day` (YMD 2025 2 1))
#ASSERT     `the day` (YMD 2025 2 1)  `falls within the period` (`the test period` 1 `Calendar months` `from a day` (YMD 2025 2 1))
#ASSERT     `the day` (YMD 2025 2 28) `falls within the period` (`the test period` 1 `Calendar months` `from a day` (YMD 2025 2 1))
#ASSERT NOT `the day` (YMD 2025 3 1)  `falls within the period` (`the test period` 1 `Calendar months` `from a day` (YMD 2025 2 1))
-- one month from 31 January 2025, whose last day the Act does not give: the first day is inside (s 18(h)), an earlier day is outside, a later day cannot be placed
#ASSERT     `the day` (YMD 2025 1 31) `falls within the period` (`the test period` 1 `Calendar months` `from a day` (YMD 2025 1 31))
#ASSERT NOT `the day` (YMD 2025 1 30) `falls within the period` (`the test period` 1 `Calendar months` `from a day` (YMD 2025 1 31))
#ASSERT REFUSED `the day` (YMD 2025 2 15) `falls within the period` (`the test period` 1 `Calendar months` `from a day` (YMD 2025 1 31))
-- a period counted after an event: a day before the event is outside; the event's own day and later days cannot be placed
#ASSERT NOT `the day` (YMD 2025 12 31) `falls within the period` (`the test period` 30 Days `after an event` (YMD 2026 1 1))
#ASSERT REFUSED `the day` (YMD 2026 1 1) `falls within the period` (`the test period` 30 Days `after an event` (YMD 2026 1 1))
#ASSERT REFUSED `the day` (YMD 2026 1 20) `falls within the period` (`the test period` 30 Days `after an event` (YMD 2026 1 1))

§ `The span of a period`

#ASSERT (`the span of the period` (`the test period` 30 Days `from a day` (YMD 2026 1 1)))'s `its first day` EQUALS YMD 2026 1 1
#ASSERT (`the span of the period` (`the test period` 30 Days `from a day` (YMD 2026 1 1)))'s `its last day` EQUALS YMD 2026 1 30
#ASSERT REFUSED (`the span of the period` (`the test period` 1 Years `from a day` (YMD 2025 7 16)))'s `its last day`
